Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - TLS certs - JWT pub key</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b1226ef7-0b7f-4404-8e34-7be088b9f7c5</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>830d75db-283a-4ed0-965f-bc754ea554c8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D2ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a44412bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f622eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>12bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f62</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>195</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444:12bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f62:2eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser or Cluster Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser or Cluster Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs) take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - RootCA - VMC Secrets - Overlay JWT Signing Key</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7.1ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a44412bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f622eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>12bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f62</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>194</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444:12bd7e1d-0fad-4c19-8420-9fc888b40f62:2eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Destination Data Store Cluster Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Cluster Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs) may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Cluster Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs). Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - RootCA - VMC Secrets - Overlay JWT Signing Key</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2eddba4d-7afb-4ef7-801c-4bea0dab186e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E65355a5c0-1ca3-45d0-be10-2cb6f867ff9bd1c22364-ee3e-4abe-836e-a63607a848cd3d4779e1-4e55-4a4d-94ca-44fc5344fe0b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>2bc9cc67-490d-4caa-9ef6-6686c5966aeb</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>d1c22364-ee3e-4abe-836e-a63607a848cd</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>747</b:Id><b:Interacti