acontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>bdce2566-0bf1-4b75-8d99-fafa39f90d47</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>719</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444:bdce2566-0bf1-4b75-8d99-fafa39f90d47:358058b8-aff1-4540-a333-ed6013f11972</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser or Node Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser or Node Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs) take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - TLS Server Cert - Overlay JWT pub key pool cache - PowerShell </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>358058b8-aff1-4540-a333-ed6013f11972</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7.1ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444bdce2566-0bf1-4b75-8d99-fafa39f90d47358058b8-aff1-4540-a333-ed6013f11972</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>bdce2566-0bf1-4b75-8d99-fafa39f90d47</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>718</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444:bdce2566-0bf1-4b75-8d99-fafa39f90d47:358058b8-aff1-4540-a333-ed6013f11972</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Destination Data Store Node Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Node Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs) may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Node Storage (VMOUser/Admin ACLs). Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - TLS Server Cert - Overlay JWT pub key pool cache - PowerShell </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>358058b8-aff1-4540-a333-ed6013f11972</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E621eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>188</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>21eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc:36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425:ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>azlocal-overlay extension may be able to remotely execute code for azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>gRPC (TLS+JWT)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>21eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E721eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>189</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>21eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc:36b57e5c-e957-4029-89e4-5bb16a017425:ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser in order to change the flow of program execution within azlocal-vmo RunAs: VMOUser to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>gRPC (TLS+JWT)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>21eea06e-5756-4957-b802-7c19e81522bc</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>ab5adec4-c498-44e0-938a-ff12cbd7a444</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D2b1226ef7-0b7f-4404-8e34-7be088b9f7c552b32604-d08d-4b38-b42b-9a0a4dcd9106830d75db-283a-4ed0-965f-bc754ea554c8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f2963659-3f3c-4bde-aadb-d2b6df386b61</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>52b32604-d08d-4b38-b42b-9a0a4dcd9106</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>197</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>b1226ef7-0b7f-4404-8e34-7be088b9f7c5:52b32604-d08d-4b38-b42b-9a0a4dcd9106:830d75db-283a-4ed0-965f-bc754ea554c8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for azlocal-vmc RunAs: admin or File System (Admin ACLs)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does azlocal-vmc RunAs: admin or File System (Admin ACLs) take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Stores: - TLS certs - JWT pub key</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b1226ef7-0b7f-4404-8e34-7be088b9f7c5</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>830d75db-283a-4ed0-965f-bc754ea554c8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E59e7be672-1875-4b89-ad8a-19813870fe65105303fe-ab88-4450-b25a-29c6e2b744713d4779e1-4e55-4a4d-94ca-44fc5344fe0b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>2bc9cc67-490d-4caa-9ef6-6686c5966aeb</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>105303fe-ab88-4450-b25a-29c6e2b74471</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>730</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9e7be672-1875-4b89-ad8a-19813870fe65:105303fe-ab88-4450-b25a-29c6e2b74471:3d4779e1-4e55-4a4d-94ca-44fc5344fe0b</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Kubernetes API Server may be able to impersonate the context of azlocal-overlay extension in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From azlocal-overlay extension to Kubernetes API Server via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9e7be672-1875-4b89-ad8a-19813870fe65</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>3d4779e1-4e55-4a4d-94ca-44fc5344fe0b</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D45355a5c0-1ca3-45d0-be10-2cb6f867ff9bd1c22364-ee3e-4abe-836e-a63607a848cd3d4779e1-4e55-4a4d-94ca-44fc5344fe0b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>2bc9cc67-490d-4caa-9ef6-6686c5966aeb</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>d1c22364-ee3e-4abe-836e-a63607a848cd</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>745</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5355a5c0-1ca3-45d0-be10-2cb6f867ff9b:d1c22364-ee3e-4abe-836e-a63607a848cd:3d4779e1-